name: Catalog preview reads metadata without model setup or Map completion
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/catalog_preview.py @TMP_TARGET @ART prepare
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
paste-file: @ART/preview-command.txt
keys: Enter
submit: logs
require-live-snap: 25 planned 1 of 2 | preview-completed
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/catalog_preview.py @TMP_TARGET @ART planned
paste-file: @ART/replay-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Outcome · completed | preview-receipt
ask: Does the receipt distinguish catalog planning from execution, retain unsupported entries, and avoid asking for a model or completing Map?
resize: 160x48
live-snap: preview-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: preview-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: preview-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: preview-60x20
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 20 Outcome · completed | preview-40x12
keys: NPage NPage
live-snap: preview-detail-40x12
ask: Can the planning-only outcome and its limits be understood at each size with predictable paging?
resize: 120x36
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/catalog_preview.py @TMP_TARGET @ART break-catalog
paste-file: @ART/preview-command.txt
keys: Enter
submit: logs
require-live-snap: 25 invalid TOML | invalid-catalog
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/catalog_preview.py @TMP_TARGET @ART failed
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/catalog_preview.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restore-catalog
paste-file: @ART/replay-command.txt
keys: Enter
keys: PPage PPage
require-live-snap: 20 Outcome · completed | earlier-preview-retained
ask: Does a malformed catalog produce a useful failure while leaving the earlier plan and ordinary investigation state intact?
keys: C-c
require-live-snap: 10 CONFIRM SESSION EXIT | explicit-quit
keys: y
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 SETUP | restarted-setup
paste-file: @ART/replay-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Outcome · completed | recovered-preview
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/catalog_preview.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restart
ask: Does no-color restart retain the same preview and failed attempt, remain in Setup, and start no model or child work?
keys: C-c
require-live-snap: 10 CONFIRM SESSION EXIT | explicit-restart-quit
keys: y
require-exit: 10
